          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+boundary"} manifolds with boundary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            %em boundary conformal field theory
            (often abbreviated as BCFT).
          %p
            For the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            understood as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            with prescribed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            = succeed "-perspective" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            are interpreted as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            may “end on”.
          %p
            In this way 2d BCFT can serve to give an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            may be described this way as boundary conditions for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFTs"} 2d CFTs
            describing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            propagating in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
          %p
            A key tool of BCFT is the
            %em boundary state
            formalism, where one interprets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+states"} coherent states
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed string
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} massive
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitons"} gravitons
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed string
          %p
            It has been argued that, therefore, for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of BCFT boundary states under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            should reproduce the expected classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            by the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"}> equivariant
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            (
            %a{:href => "#Moore03"}> Moore 03, section 3
            ).
          %p
            While this gives, in principle, a precise algebraic definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            from the
            = succeed "-perspective," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            of the boundary states. The proposal has been checked in some special cases (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BraunSchaeferNameki05"} Braun &amp; Schaefer-Nameki 05
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#QuirozStefanski01"} Quiroz-Stefanski 01
          %p
            Specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            at
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
            the relevant boundary states are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sums"} sums
            of boundary states for each “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            \-twisted sector” of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed string
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            up to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the element
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TwistedSector.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#BCR00"} BCR 00
          %p
            Here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            of the
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_V(g)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character"} character
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_V
            of some
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi KU
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in R_{\mathbb{C}}(G) = KU_G(\ast)
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RecknagelSchomerus13"} Recknagel-Schomerus 13 (4.102)
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RG-flow"} RG-flow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of the boundary states for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            do coincide with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi KU
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU_G(\ast) = R_{\mathbb{C}}(G)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            singularity (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %blockquote
            %p But maybe this has not yet been actually proven?
          %h2#results Results
          %p
            There are some mistakes in the literature. A clean account is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FuchsSchweigertWalcher00"} Fuchs-Schweigert-Walcher 00
            %a{:href => "#FuchsKasteLercheLutkenSchweigert00"} Fuchs-Kaste-Lerche-Lutken-Schweigert 00
          %h2#computer_scan_of_gepnermodel_compactifications Computer scan of Gepner-model compactifications
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            with non-geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            such that the would-be string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            with these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spaces"} target spaces
            are in fact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+models"} Gepner models
            (in the sense of
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.physicsforums.com/insights/spectral-standard-model-string-compactifications/"} Spectral Standard Model and String Compactifications
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04a"} Dijkstra-Huiszoon-Schellekens 04a
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04b"} Dijkstra-Huiszoon-Schellekens 04b
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SchellekensSuperGepnerModelScanII.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              A plot of
              = succeed "-like" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
              in a computer scan of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
              according to
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04b"} Dijkstra-Huiszoon-Schellekens 04b
            %p
              The blue dot indicates the couplings in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 5
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
              theory. The faint lines are NOT drawn by hand, but reflect increased density of Gepner models as seen by the computer scan.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+brane"}> fractional brane
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+brane"} permutation brane
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th singularity
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory+with+singularities"} field theory with singularities
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+condition"}> boundary condition
                    \/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+wall"}> domain wall
                    \/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-brane"} bi-brane
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} QFT with defects
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The boundary state formalism in BCFT is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                C. G. Callan, C. Lovelace, C. R. Nappi and S. A. Yost,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adding holes and crosscaps to the superstring
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(87)90065-4"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(87)90065-4
            %li
              %p
                C. G. Callan, C. Lovelace, C. R. Nappi and S. A. Yost,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Loop corrections to superstring equations of motion
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Scott_Yost/publication/222468211_Loop_Corrections_to_Superstring_Equations_of_Motion/links/5a54d5eda6fdccd72f5b4583/Loop-Corrections-to-Superstring-Equations-of-Motion.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                N. Ishibashi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Boundary and Crosscap States in Conformal Field Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inis.iaea.org/collection/NCLCollectionStore/_Public/20/072/20072844.pdf#page=125"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                N. Ishibashi and T. Onogi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Open string model building
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(89)90054-0"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(89)90054-0
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DixonFriedanMartinecShenker87"} Dixon-Friedan-Martinec-Shenker 87
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#RecknagelSchomerus99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Recknagel"}> Andreas Recknagel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Schomerus"} Volker Schomerus
              = succeed "," do
                %em Boundary Deformation Theory and Moduli Spaces of D-Branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9811237"} arXiv:hep-th/9811237
          %p Textbook accounts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Plauschinn"} Erik Plauschinn
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Conformal Field Theory – With Applications to String Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 779
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-00450-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-00450-6
            %li#RecknagelSchomerus13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Recknagel"}> Andreas Recknagel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Schomerus"} Volker Schomerus
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Boundary Conformal Field Theory and the Worldsheet Approach to D-branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1308990"} spire:1308990
          %h3#relation_to_ktheory Relation to K-theory
          %p
            The suggestion that
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of boundary states in 2d BCFT should realize the expected classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"}> equivariant
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            apparntly goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Moore03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"}> Gregory Moore
              , section 3 of
              %em K-Theory from a physical perspective
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0304018"}> arXiv:hep-th/0304018
              )
          %p This has been checked in examples in
          %ul
            %li#BraunSchaeferNameki05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Braun"}> Volker Braun
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakura+Schafer-Nameki"} Sakura Schafer-Nameki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-Brane Charges in Gepner Models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0511100"} arXiv:hep-th/0511100
            %li#KrizZayasQuiroz08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"}> Igor Kriz
                , Leopoldo A. Pando Zayas, Norma Quiroz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Comments on D-branes on Orbifolds and K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0703122"} arXiv:hep-th/0703122
          %p A mismatch was claimed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#QuirozStefanski01"} Quiroz-Stefanski 01
          %h3#for_rational_cft_wzw_models_and_gepner_models For rational CFT, WZW models and Gepner models
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+CFT"} rational CFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+models"} Gepner models
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+models"} WZW models
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Brunner"}> Ilka Brunner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"} Michael Douglas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-branes on the Quintic
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9906200"} arXiv:hep-th/9906200
            %li#FuchsSchweigertWalcher00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Projections in string theory and boundary states for Gepner models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0003298"} arXiv:hep-th/0003298
              %p
                (with emphasis on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GSO+projections"} GSO projections
            %li#FuchsKasteLercheLutkenSchweigert00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
                , P. Kaste,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"} Wolfgang Lerche
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Boundary Fixed Points, Enhanced Gauge Symmetry and Singular Bundles on K3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0007145"} arXiv:hep-th/0007145
              %p
                (with emphasis on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
                on coincident D-branes)
            %li
              %p
                Sergei E. Parkhomenko,
                %em Free Field Construction of D-Branes in Rational Models of CFT and Gepner Models
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0802.3445"}> arXiv:0802.3445
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"}> Giovanni Felder
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"} Jürg Fröhlich
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"} Jürgen Fuchs
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
                %em The geometry of WZW branes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9909030"}> arXiv:hep-th/9909030
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#BraunSchaeferNameki05"} Braun &amp; Schaefer-Nameki 05
          %h3#on_orbifolds On orbifolds
          %p
            Discussion specifically concerning
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            includes
          %ul
            %li#DixonFriedanMartinecShenker87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lance+Dixon"}> Lance Dixon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Friedan"} Daniel Friedan
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Martinec"} Emil Martinec
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Shenker"} Stephen Shenker
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The conformal field theory of orbifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(87)90676-6"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(87)90676-6
            %li#DiaconescuGomis99
              %p
                Diaconescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaume+Gomis"} Jaume Gomis
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fractional Branes and Boundary States in Orbifold Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9906242"} arXiv:hep-th/9906242
            %li#BCR00
              %p
                M. Billo’, B. Craps, F. Roose,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orbifold boundary states from Cardy’s condition
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0011060"} arXiv:hep-th/0011060
            %li#QuirozStefanski01
              %p
                N. Quiroz,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bogdan+Stefanski"} Bogdan Stefanski
                Jr,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirichlet Branes on Orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0110041"} arXiv:hep-th/0110041
            %li#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04a
              %p
                T.P.T. Dijkstra, L. R. Huiszoon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Schellekens"} Bert Schellekens
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral Supersymmetric Standard Model Spectra from Orientifolds of Gepner Models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0403196"} arXiv:hep-th/0403196
            %li#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04b
              %p
                T.P.T. Dijkstra, L. R. Huiszoon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Schellekens"} Bert Schellekens
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric Standard Model Spectra from RCFT orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0411129"} arXiv:hep-th/0411129
            %li#MMR06
              %p
                Jaydeep Majumder, Subir Mukhopadhyay, Koushik Ray,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fractional Branes in Non-compact Type IIA Orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0602135"} arXiv:hep-th/0602135
